{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The completion verifier returns a DEPENDENCY-LINK record where a `CompletionVerdict` belongs, blocking the close\n\n## Reproduced deterministically, twice\n\n`rebar transition b586-2fda-8a15-4260 in_progress closed`, exit 1, fail-closed (no verdict, no\nsignature, close refused — correct behaviour for an unusable verdict):\n\n```\ncompletion verification workflow did not produce a verdict:\n  step 'decide@then/verify' failed: structured output failed validation:\n  1 validation error for CompletionVerdict\nverdict\n  Field required [type=missing, input_value={'relation': 'depends_on'...: 'f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31'}, input_type=dict]\n```\n\nTwo consecutive attempts, both failing at the same step, each returning a TICKET-LINK record\nfrom the ticket's own graph in the slot where the verdict schema is expected (attempt 1\ncarried `link_uuid`, attempt 2 `relation: depends_on`, both naming `f2f3-9cb1-335b-4e31`).\n\n## Root cause (isolated; full trail in comments)\n\nThe extraction is schema-BLIND: `tolerant_parse` (src/rebar/llm/structured.py:121) returns the\nFIRST parseable JSON object — fenced blocks first (`_FENCE_RE`, :40), then the first balanced\nobject (`_first_json_object`, :82). The verifier's agentic transcript quotes dep-link records\nfrom `show_ticket` tool results, and the model restates one before its verdict; the quoted\nrecord wins. Trigger isolation is DONE (original AC #1): E3 replayed the captured reply\ndeterministically with and without the quoted dep record — with it, 3 of 4 layout variants\nfail today; without it, all parse (experiment-results comment). Fifth recurrence of this\nclass; instance history in the design-investigation comment.\n\n## Approach\n\nSchema-filtered candidate selection in `parse_structured` (src/rebar/llm/structured.py:212) —\nNOT in `tolerant_parse` (:121), whose `schema` parameter already means json-repair guidance\nand whose first-object, schema-less contract is pinned\n(tests/unit/test_structured.py::test_tolerant_parse_first_object_wins_on_multi_object).\n\nSelection: enumerate candidates — every fenced block (models fence-wrap quoted records;\nmeasured, E2 catch 2), every top-level non-overlapping balanced object (cap: keep the LAST\n32), plus the array-unwrap forms `validate_to` (:177) already accepts. Screen each by\nkey-overlap against `model_cls.model_fields` — mandatory, because all-defaults contracts in\nsrc/rebar/llm/contracts.py (e.g. the models `default_outputs` at :43 iterates) validate `{}`.\nValidate each survivor via `validate_to`; the LAST valid candidate wins; when >=2 validate and\nlast != first, log a warning naming both. No valid candidate -> fall back byte-for-byte to\ntoday's pipeline so the error message and retry behavior are unchanged.\n\nRationale (G6): last-valid-wins recovers all five historical recurrence layouts (payload\nrendered last in each; E3), matches instructor's last-wins prompt-injection posture, and\ncoheres with the sentinel channel's last-block rule landing in the follow-on story. The\none-call-repair pin and `OUTPUT_RETRIES` (:292) reask loop are untouched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/structured.py — candidate selection in `parse_structured`; `tolerant_parse`\n  untouched\n- tests/unit/test_structured.py — new pins (corpus replay, last-wins warning, fallback)\n- tests/fixtures/ (new corpus file(s)) — the captured b586 verifier reply + 3 layout variants\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier (real reply text -> real parser -> validated contract object; per the shared\ntest-design standard, this crosses every component of the proven mechanism in-process):\n\n- RED-first corpus replay: the captured b586-shape reply in 4 recorded layout variants — 3\n  fail on today's parser, all 4 must pass after.\n- Property test: generated prose + schema-valid decoys with the payload rendered last parses\n  to the contract (seed 20250804, n=500 — the E3 prototype ran 500/500).\n- Mutation check: re-introducing first-wins selection turns the corpus test RED.\n- Negative controls: the schema-less `tolerant_parse` pin is unchanged; the full existing\n  tests/unit/test_structured.py suite passes unmodified (E3 measured 110/110 with the\n  prototype injected).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The captured b586-shape reply (quoted dep record before the verdict) parses to a\n      `CompletionVerdict` in all 4 recorded layout variants — checked by the new corpus tests\n      in tests/unit/test_structured.py.\n- [ ] When >=2 candidates validate and last != first, a warning is logged naming both — checked\n      by a caplog unit test.\n- [ ] A reply with no schema-valid candidate falls back to today's pipeline byte-for-byte\n      (same exception type and message) — checked by a pinned fallback test reusing an\n      existing failure fixture.\n- [ ] All pre-existing tests/unit/test_structured.py pins pass unmodified — checked by running\n      that file's suite under `make test`'s runner.\n- [ ] The remedy for the original failure is this parser fix, not `--force-close` (original AC\n      #5) — checked by the corpus test asserting the verdict validates.","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785891907564219001,"uuid":"256f3757-88d5-4d17-b730-2a5e817314cb"}